==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sunny Celeboodle]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 4~10 seconds<sup>120f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Lucky Sloth]] spawns.
**1 [[Marching Kory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Save up your money and upgrade your [[Worker Cat]] to level 8 and get max money before attacking the base. Then stall the peons using [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall]]. After Martin and Celeboodle appear, stop stalling and lure them to your base to an area where they're close but not hitting the base. Luring them closer to your base will help, because since Lucky Sloth is very slow, and Sunny Celeboodle and Martin aren't, giving you a good amount of time to save up money, then stack [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]], it will give you a good amount of cash after killing the two. Use 2-3 meatshields and some long range support. Dragon/King Dragon may help deal with the sloth. Use [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon]] if possible.

